//! error/traits — Error trait definitions.
//!
//! Status: reserved (M4+, stdlib/SPEC.md §4 / C4).
//!
//! Trait-based error handling is explicitly out of scope for M3: the
//! language has no `trait`/`impl` method dispatch today (SPEC.md C4),
//! and there is no `Error` trait (SPEC.md §4: E stays an ordinary type).
//! All error behavior is expressed through free functions and the
//! language's built-in `panic`, `Option`, and `Result` (E1–E3), plus
//! `?` / `??` for propagation (E4).
//!
//! Future design (M4, when traits land):
//! - A `trait Display` for rendering error values.
//! - A `trait Error` sub-trait carrying `fn message(&self) -> String`.
//! - `impl Error for <typed enum>` per error category.
//!
//! Unblock condition: trait/impl support (SPEC.md C4) + typed error
//! enums from `error/types.nv`.
